# Background — the live flow you are completing
The per-phase gate table already landed in `ngv2/gate_executor.py` (separate, green
concern — do NOT touch it). `run_gates(from_phase, to_phase, evidence)` now gates EVERY
consecutive transition fail-closed: each transition requires its leaving-phase evidence
key present/non-empty in `evidence`, else `advance` is False. The conductor
(`ngv2/hunt_conductor.py::run_conductor_step`) does `evidence = build_evidence(state)`
then `run_gates(state['phase'], target_phase, evidence)` and advances iff `advance`.
`build_evidence` is the nested closure inside `build_default_seams`; today it emits ONLY
the poc/detonate keys, NOT the per-phase gate keys the gate table requires, so the live
FSM deadlocks at the first transition. This brief makes `build_evidence` ALSO derive the
8 source-derived keys (incl. `source_ready`) and thread the leaving-phase boolean flags
forward from `state['evidence']`, so the FSM traverses. (See "The target contract" for
the precise split — the booleans are NOT among the 8 source-derived keys.)

