# The target contract — what build_evidence MUST emit
`build_evidence(state)` returns a FLAT dict for `run_gates`. It TRANSLATES `state`
into the gate vocabulary — it must NOT copy `state['evidence']` forward verbatim, and
it must NOT unconditionally overwrite the leaving-phase boolean flags with an
artifacts-scan. There are TWO distinct families of keys, and they are derived
DIFFERENTLY: the 8 SOURCE-DERIVED keys (always computed from `state`), and the
leaving-phase BOOLEAN FLAGS (threaded from `state['evidence']` when present, omitted
otherwise). The committed oracle
`tests/ngv2/test_p11_build_evidence_perphase.py` (faithful, UNCHANGED) is the
authoritative contract and pins exactly this split.

THE 8 SOURCE-DERIVED KEYS — and ONLY these when `state['evidence']` carries no
boolean flags (the oracle's `test_oracle_build_evidence_emits_eight_keys` asserts
`set(ev.keys()) == {poc_source, target_import_names, target_source, expected_signature,
sink_name, call_sites, detonation_report, source_ready}` when `state['evidence']`
holds ONLY `detonation_report_raw`):

| Evidence key | build_evidence derivation |
|---|---|
| `poc_source` | from `state['parked_package']['poc']` |
| `target_import_names` | MUST include package names AST-parsed from `poc_source` (so a PoC importing the target package matches even when `state['target']` differs) |
| `target_source` | MUST contain `expected_signature`; if the repo source file does not contain the sink signature, fall back to using `expected_signature` itself as `target_source` |
| `expected_signature` | from the finding |
| `sink_name` | from the finding |
| `call_sites` | from the finding |
| `detonation_report` | computed by mapping `state['evidence']['detonation_report_raw']` through the detonation gate; then the raw key is DROPPED (NEVER emit `detonation_report_raw`) |
| `source_ready` | `= bool(state.get('repo'))`, ALWAYS emitted, derived from repo presence (NOT from findings) |

THE LEAVING-PHASE BOOLEAN / FLAG KEYS (`findings`, `triage_result`, `verify_result`,
`novelty_result`, `report_artifact`, `approval`, `submission_result`):

- These are NOT among the 8 source-derived keys. They MUST be ABSENT from the output
  when `state['evidence']` lacks them (this is what makes the eight-keys assertion hold
  and what keeps `run_gates` failing-closed on an empty state).
- Thread each one into the output FROM `state['evidence']` WHEN it is present there
  (the oracle's `test_oracle_full_state_advances_all_transitions` populates each of
  these as a positive value inside `state['evidence']` and requires every transition to
  advance — so the impl MUST surface them from `state['evidence']`, not clobber them).
- They MAY ALSO be sourced from an artifacts-scan-by-phase (`state['artifacts']`
  discriminated by `art['data']['phase']`) as a SECONDARY fallback, but ONLY when such
  an artifact actually exists — an artifacts-scan must NEVER overwrite a value already
  present in `state['evidence']`, and must NEVER inject a `None`/placeholder.
- When a flag is in NEITHER `state['evidence']` NOR present as a real artifact, it MUST
  be OMITTED entirely (absent), never set to `None`. A present-`None` bypasses
  `run_gates`' missing-key guard and breaks fail-closed; and an extra key breaks the
  exactly-8 assertion.

MANDATORY RULES (each is load-bearing for a committed-oracle assertion):
1. An underivable key MUST be OMITTED, never set to `None`.
2. NEVER emit `detonation_report_raw` in the output (compute `detonation_report`, drop
   the raw key).
3. `target_import_names` MUST include names AST-parsed from `poc_source`.
4. `target_source` MUST contain `expected_signature`; fall back to `expected_signature`
   if the repo file lacks the sink.
5. Boolean flags are threaded from `state['evidence']` when present (an artifacts-scan
   is a NON-OVERWRITING secondary source only), and OMITTED when absent.

DO NOT hand-author a concrete `build_evidence` body here — the synthesizer derives the
implementation from this corrected spec plus the committed oracle. The whole point of
this brief is that the GREEN oracle and the live FSM drive the SAME translating
implementation: source-derived keys computed from `state`, boolean flags threaded
forward from `state['evidence']`.

